# weewx-influxdb.service -- InfluxDB 2.x on marvin, the weewx tenant's store (S124, DEC-0141)
#
# WHAT THIS REPLACES
# ------------------
# The `influxdb` service of Foundation's (the DS918+) `docker-compose.yml`, project
# `weewx-rtldavis`: image `influxdb:2.7` (resolved to v2.7.12 on 2026-06-19),
# bind mounts `/volume1/docker/influxdb/{data,config}`, port 8086 published to
# the LAN, restart `unless-stopped`, DSM `db` log driver. It is the last weather
# workload left on Foundation (ops#260 step 3 / OPS-DEC-0188); its three
# consumers -- weewx's `influx.py` uploader, eh-proxy `/query`, dashboard's
# hourly `event-detect` -- all already run on marvin and reach it by Foundation's
# LAN IP. docs/INFLUXDB-MIGRATION.md is the runbook this unit is one piece of.
#
# WHY IT IS NAMED, PLACED AND RUN THIS WAY
# ---------------------------------------
# - `weewx-influxdb` (unit AND container) sits inside the weewx tenant manifest's
#   globs (`units = weewx*.service`, `containers = *weewx*`), so `t-weewx` gets
#   start/stop/restart/logs/inspect/journal through `marvinctl` with NO manifest
#   change and no new grant. InfluxDB stays weewx-owned, as ops#260 arbitrated
#   (weewx executes, marvin hosts); dashboard's `eh_rollup` bucket and its
#   `eh-daily-rollup` Task live inside it unchanged (dashboard DEC-0266 / weewx
#   DEC-0100).
# - `influxdb:2.7.12`, not `:2.7`, and `--pull=never`: the exact engine version
#   Foundation runs. Dashboard's Flux task was verified against THIS engine's
#   boundary semantics (their influx/README.md §1 refuses to install on a changed
#   engine) -- a floating tag could silently bump it at the first pull. The
#   owner pulls the image once at install; a missing tag then fails loudly.
# - `--user 996:986` is `t-weewx`. Foundation's data dir is owned by uid 1000
#   because the official image gosu-drops to `influxdb` (1000) when started as
#   root; on marvin uid 1000 is a human account, so the tenant uid is used and
#   the copied tree is chowned to it (docs/INFLUXDB-MIGRATION.md §3). Started as
#   non-root the image skips its init/gosu path and runs influxd directly --
#   supported upstream, and the right shape on a multi-tenant box.
# - No `DOCKER_INFLUXDB_INIT_*` variables: the copied bolt store is already
#   initialised, so they would be ignored -- and a unit never carries a secret
#   (marvin ACCESS-AUDIT-S7 A6). Tokens, org, buckets, the Task and the CLI's
#   operator config travel INSIDE the copied data/config trees, byte for byte.
# - `-p 8086:8086`: like-for-like with Foundation (LAN-published, never
#   internet-facing). eh-proxy runs on the default bridge and reaches the host's
#   LAN IP; loopback would not be reachable from it. Tightening the bind is a
#   post-move change, not a cutover rider (ops#260 migration hygiene).
# - `weather.slice`, like weewx.service: the dashboard's live surface reads this
#   store on every page load, and weewx blocks its RESTThread on it.
# - Paths under `/srv/docker/weewx/influxdb/` -- tenant tree, local NVMe
#   (COMPUTE-NODE.md §3: databases never on network storage), inside restic's
#   nightly `/srv` set. A consistent `influx backup` pre-dump timer follows AFTER
#   the move as its own change (runbook §5), the weewx-db-dump pattern.
# - `docker stop -t 60`: a clean influxd shutdown flushes the WAL. DEC-0008's
#   "kill, never stop" is a Synology-daemon hazard; every marvin unit stops.
[Unit]
Description=weewx-influxdb (InfluxDB 2.7.12 -- weewx archive store; eh_rollup + eh-daily-rollup Task inside)
Requires=docker.service
After=docker.service network-online.target
Wants=network-online.target

[Service]
Slice=weather.slice
Restart=always
RestartSec=10
TimeoutStopSec=90
ExecStartPre=-/usr/bin/docker rm -f weewx-influxdb
ExecStart=/usr/bin/docker run --rm --name weewx-influxdb --pull=never \
    --user 996:986 \
    -p 8086:8086 \
    -e TZ=America/New_York \
    -v /srv/docker/weewx/influxdb/data:/var/lib/influxdb2 \
    -v /srv/docker/weewx/influxdb/config:/etc/influxdb2 \
    influxdb:2.7.12
ExecStop=/usr/bin/docker stop -t 60 weewx-influxdb

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
